window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-1ddec1686605aee6"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"revise-a-lesson-package\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">修订整套课程材料</h1> <p>把已批准的反馈一致地应用到相互关联的文件中。</p> <p>提供当前课程文件夹、书面或口述反馈、获准修改的文件清单和确认规则，让 ChatGPT 制定修订计划、更新关联材料、保留旧版本，并返回经过核验的变更日志。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>需要同时修订演示文稿、指南、讲义和答案的教师。</li> <li>必须在多个文件间一致应用的反馈。</li> <li>需要设置审批检查点、归档旧版并记录变更的审阅工作。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>google-drive</code></td> <td>读取已批准的课程文件并保留先前版本。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>应用已批准的反馈，并生成逐文件变更日志。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>修订课程资料包</p> <p>建议模型：<code>gpt-6-astra</code> · 建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请根据这些反馈修订此文件夹中已批准的课程文件。\n\n首先，请逐个文件列出变更计划。我批准后：\n- 更新课程演示文稿、教师指南、学生讲义和答案\n- 将旧版本保存在 Archive（归档）中\n- 核对示例、说明和答案是否仍然一致\n- 创建简明的变更日志\n- 列出尚未解决的问题\n\n不要修改获批清单以外的文件。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"convert-feedback-into-a-change-plan\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">将反馈整理成变更计划</h2> <p>收集当前课程文件夹、反馈内容、已批准的文件清单，以及任何必须明确确认后才能进行的改动。区分明确要求、建议和待确认问题。</p> <p>请 ChatGPT 逐项说明每条反馈会影响哪些文件和章节。</p> <p><a id=\"approve-the-scope\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">批准修改范围</h2> <p>允许编辑前，先审阅逐文件计划。确认必须保留哪些旧版本，以及哪一个源文件负责决定术语、示例或答案等共享内容。</p> <p>获得批准后，再协调修订相互关联的文件。</p> <p><a id=\"verify-cross-file-consistency\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">核验跨文件一致性</h2> <p>对比更新后的演示文稿、教师指南、讲义和答案，检查：</p> <ul> <li>示例和答案仍然匹配</li> <li>说明使用的术语保持一致</li> <li>需要同步的时间安排变更已出现在所有相关文件中</li> <li>来源链接仍然有效</li> <li>旧版本已归档</li> <li>尚未解决的问题仍然清楚可见</li> </ul> <p>变更日志可帮助教师作最终审核。除非负责审阅的人确认，否则不要把提出的修改当成已获批准的教学或政策决定。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"revise-a-lesson-package\">Revise a lesson package</h1> <p>Apply approved feedback consistently across connected files.</p> <p>Use ChatGPT with a current lesson folder, written or dictated feedback, approved files, and confirmation rules to create a revision plan, update connected materials, preserve prior versions, and return a verified change log.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Teachers revising a deck, guide, handout, and answer key together.</li> <li>Feedback that must be applied consistently across several files.</li> <li>Reviews that need an approval checkpoint, archive, and change log.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>google-drive</code></td> <td>Read the approved lesson files and preserve prior versions.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>Apply approved feedback and produce a file-by-file change log.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Revise a Lesson Package</p> <p>Suggested model：<code>gpt-6-astra</code> · Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use this feedback to revise the approved lesson files in this folder.\n\nFirst, show me a file-by-file change plan. After I approve it:\n- update the lesson deck, teacher guide, student handout, and answer key\n- preserve prior versions in Archive\n- verify that examples, directions, and answers still match\n- create a concise change log\n- list unresolved questions\n\nDo not change files outside the approved list.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"convert-feedback-into-a-change-plan\">Convert feedback into a change plan</h2> <p>Gather the current lesson folder, the feedback, the approved file list, and any changes that require explicit confirmation. Distinguish requested changes from suggestions or open questions.</p> <p>Ask ChatGPT to map each feedback item to the files and sections it would affect.</p> <h2 id=\"approve-the-scope\">Approve the scope</h2> <p>Review the file-by-file plan before allowing edits. Confirm which prior versions must be preserved and which source file controls shared content such as terminology, examples, or answers.</p> <p>After approval, revise connected files in one coordinated pass.</p> <h2 id=\"verify-cross-file-consistency\">Verify cross-file consistency</h2> <p>Compare the updated deck, teacher guide, handout, and answer key. Check that:</p> <ul> <li>examples and answers still match</li> <li>instructions use consistent terms</li> <li>timing changes appear everywhere they should</li> <li>source links remain intact</li> <li>prior versions are archived</li> <li>unresolved questions remain visible</li> </ul> <p>Use the change log to support a final educator review. Do not treat requested edits as approved instructional or policy decisions unless the responsible reviewer confirms them.</p>"};
